    "created_at": "2024-11-22T05:19:30Z",
    "updated_at": "2024-11-22T05:19:30Z",
    "body": "Ah, yep, overzealous catching of exceptions is precisely one of the ways the reference implementation can be buggy compared to the spec. (In the spec, \"performing\" a null algorithm is undefined behavior, whereas in JS it's just a catchable exception.)\r\n\r\nThanks for investigating; one of the editors (possibly myself) will work on trying to find a good solution here soon.",
